<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" target="ai_agent_systemic_risks::cyber_exploit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased kinetic/aerial strikes prompt adversaries to shift to and escalate cyber operations (to degrade sensors, comms, and C2) and to exploit disrupted systems, raising the frequency of successful compromises of AI-dependent infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_agent_systemic_risks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" target="global_bond_market_shock::corporate_credit_spreads" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid increase in strikes causes immediate revenue disruption, supply-chain interruption and elevated default and liquidity risk for firms in the combat zone and their suppliers, which raises risk premia and widens corporate bond spreads.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" target="us_china_strategic_rival::policymaker_trust" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp uptick in Russian strikes raises US demands that China use its leverage to restrain Moscow, and if Beijing does not take visible action the result is an observable decline in US policymakers' trust in Chinese commitments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
