<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_flows" target="global_bond_market_shock::equity_valuation_multipl" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_flows" target="global_bond_market_shock::currency_strength" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_flows" target="ai_agent_systemic_risks::exposure_concentration" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">During bond-market stress, cross-border capital rebalances toward large, liquid incumbents and safe-haven jurisdictions, channeling investment and contracts into a smaller set of AI providers and infrastructure providers and thereby increasing concentration of economic and operational exposure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_agent_systemic_risks</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_flows" target="iran_hormuz_flashpoint::supply_risk_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Net capital outflows (a fall in cross-border inflows) reduce available financing for traders and insurers and raise counterparty/default concerns, which markets translate quickly into higher market-implied expectations of future oil-supply risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::investor_confidence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp reversals or reductions in cross-border capital flows withdraw financing, force local asset sales and increase risk premia in the region, directly lowering investor confidence in Ukraine/Russia-exposed assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_market_shock::cross_border_flows" target="us_china_strategic_rival::policymaker_trust" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, asymmetric capital flight or abrupt reversals interpreted as financial coercion reduce mutual confidence that each side will honor market‑access and investment commitments, directly lowering trust between US and Chinese policymakers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
