<edge source="ai_agent_systemic_risks::agent_deployment_rate" target="iran_hormuz_flashpoint::maritime_attack_frequenc" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Faster deployment of autonomous/AI-enabled drones, unmanned surface vessels, and precision guidance tools widens operational capacity for state proxies or irregular forces to mount more frequent deniable strikes against commercial shipping.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_agent_systemic_risks</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_agent_systemic_risks::agent_deployment_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Faster operational deployment of autonomous and semi-autonomous weaponized agents (loitering munitions, strike drones, swarms) increases the number of platforms available for attacks, raising the observed rate of kinetic and aerial strikes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_agent_systemic_risks</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_agent_systemic_risks::agent_deployment_rate" target="us_china_strategic_rival::diplomatic_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid rollouts of agentic systems (especially in contested domains or dual‑use sectors) create new bilateral incidents, policy disputes, or coordination needs that drive more frequent high‑level consultations and crisis‑management meetings between the US and China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_agent_systemic_risks</data>
